WEBVTT

00:04:59.251 --> 00:05:00.640
on his visit to MIT,

00:05:00.664 --> 00:05:02.962
and I really wanted to give
him a periodic table.

00:05:02.986 --> 00:05:05.328
So I stayed up at night
and talked to my husband,

00:05:05.352 --> 00:05:07.608
"How do I give President Obama
a periodic table?

00:05:07.632 --> 00:05:09.700
What if he says,
'Oh, I already have one,'

00:05:09.724 --> 00:05:11.364
or, 'I've already memorized it?'"

00:05:11.388 --> 00:05:12.396
(Laughter)

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:15.700
So he came to visit my lab and looked
around -- it was a great visit.

00:05:15.724 --> 00:05:17.058
And then afterward, I said,

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:19.445
"Sir, I want to give you
the periodic table,

00:05:19.469 --> 00:05:22.832
in case you're ever in a bind
and need to calculate molecular weight."

00:05:22.856 --> 00:05:23.942
(Laughter)

00:05:23.966 --> 00:05:27.480
I thought "molecular weight" sounded
much less nerdy than "molar mass."

00:05:27.504 --> 00:05:28.575
(Laughter)

00:05:28.599 --> 00:05:31.498
And he looked at it and said,